    "description": "Pattern develops, owns, and operates wind, solar, storage, and transmission infrastructure across North America and selected international markets. Its customers are utilities, corporate offtakers, and power markets that contract for renewable energy, capacity, and transmission services under long-duration arrangements. The company follows an asset-heavy independent power producer and developer model with a mix of operating projects and a large development pipeline. Public disclosures describe more than 6 gigawatts of operating capacity and a development portfolio that includes major transmission-led growth projects such as SunZia. Pattern was taken private in 2020 and has continued to add long-duration institutional capital to support development and operating growth. A consortium led by APG and Australian Retirement Trust acquired Riverstone's equity stake in 2025 and joined CPP Investments and management as owners, while exact ownership percentages were not publicly disclosed.",
